#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:1
msgid "Load the Moon relief dataset in various resolutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:7
msgid "Moon relief dataset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:9
msgid ""
"This function downloads the dataset from the GMT data server, caches it in a "
"user data directory (usually ``~/.gmt/server/moon/moon_relief/``), and load "
"the dataset as an :class:`xarray.DataArray`. An internet connection is "
"required the first time around, but subsequent calls will load the dataset "
"from the local data directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:14
msgid ""
"The dataset can also be accessed by specifying a file name in any grid "
"processing function or plotting method, using the following file name "
"format: **@moon_relief**\\_\\ *res*\\_\\ *reg*. *res* is the grid "
"resolution; *reg* is the grid registration type (**p** for pixel "
"registration, **g** for gridline registration). If *reg* is omitted (e.g., "
"``@moon_relief_01d``), the gridline-registered grid will be loaded for grid "
"processing functions and the pixel-registered grid will be loaded for "
"plotting functions. If *res* is also omitted (i.e., ``@moon_relief``), GMT "
"automatically selects a suitable resolution based on the current region and "
"projection settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:24
msgid ""
"This dataset comes with a color palette table (CPT) file, ``@moon_relief."
"cpt``. To use the dataset-specific CPT when plotting the dataset, explicitly "
"set ``cmap=\"@moon_relief.cpt\"``, otherwise GMT's default CPT (*google/"
"turbo*) will be used. If the dataset is referenced by the file name in a "
"grid plotting method, the dataset-specific CPT file is used automatically "
"unless another CPT is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:30
msgid ""
"Refer to :gmt-datasets:`moon-relief.html` for more details about available "
"datasets, including version information and references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:34
msgid ""
"The grid resolution. The suffix ``d``, ``m`` and ``s`` stand for arc-"
"degrees, arc-minutes and arc-seconds. Note that ``\"14s\"`` refers to a "
"resolution of 14.0625 arc-seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:38
msgid ""
"The subregion of the grid to load, in the form of a sequence [*xmin*, "
"*xmax*, *ymin*, *ymax*] or an ISO country code. Required for grids with "
"resolutions higher than 5 arc-minutes (i.e., ``\"05m\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/moon_relief.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.moon_relief.load_moon_relief:42
msgid ""
"Grid registration type. Either ``\"pixel\"`` for pixel registration or "
"``\"gridline\"`` for gridline registration. Default is ``None``, which means "
"``\"gridline\"`` for all resolutions except for ``\"14s\"`` which is "
"``\"pixel\"`` only."
msgstr ""

